CALL newPutForth(367, 1, 'Social media has made public life angrier, dumber, and more divided. The incentive structure is designed to maximize outrage and engagement — two things that are the same thing. Nobody would have built it this way if they\'d understood what they were building.');
CALL newPutForth(465, 1, 'The mainstream media\'s job is supposed to be accountability journalism. What it\'s become is a brand — politically reliable, ideologically consistent, and deeply incurious about anything that challenges the worldview of its audience. That\'s not journalism. That\'s content.');
CALL newPutForth(498, 1, 'Facebook has systematically suppressed conservative content — conservative news, conservative groups, conservative figures — while letting left-wing outrage campaigns operate with impunity. The evidence isn\'t anecdotal. It\'s documented. And they\'ve been doing it for years.');
CALL newPutForth(504, 1, 'Expertise matters. Someone who has spent 30 years studying a subject knows more about it than someone who read three articles. That\'s not elitism — that\'s the reason we have experts. Trust them in their domain.');
CALL newPutForth(1249, 1, 'The media figured out that outrage pays. A story that makes you angry keeps you on the page longer, generates more shares, and sells more ads than a story that informs you. So they produce more of what angers you. It\'s a machine optimizing for your worst instincts.');
CALL newPutForth(1505, 1, 'The internet was supposed to democratize information and connect humanity. Instead, big tech consolidated control, governments found new levers, and the most powerful communications medium in history became a polarization machine and an ad-delivery system. Disappointing is an understatement.');
CALL newPutForth(1508, 1, 'The early internet was genuinely open — chaotic, but free. Gradually, through terms-of-service changes, app store monopolies, and regulatory capture, the major platforms have reasserted a control over speech that puts any traditional editor to shame. And they did it invisibly.');
CALL newPutForth(1513, 1, 'Most herbal remedies don\'t work. The few that do got tested and turned into actual medicine with dosage requirements and clinical evidence. What\'s left in the supplement aisle is prayer in a capsule — and the FTC should treat it accordingly.');
CALL newPutForth(1517, 1, 'The First Amendment exists to protect speech that might be false, offensive, or wrong — because the alternative is letting someone else decide what\'s true. But it was never meant to protect deliberate fraud or defamation, and we shouldn\'t pretend it does.');




